# Practical 8 – Matrix Chain Multiplication using Dynamic Programming

## Aim

To implement the **Matrix Chain Multiplication Problem using Dynamic Programming** in Python.

## Description

The Matrix Chain Multiplication Problem finds the **best order to multiply a sequence of matrices** so that the total number of scalar multiplications is minimum.

The program uses Dynamic Programming to store previously calculated results and avoid repeated calculations.

## Sample Input

```text
Enter matrix dimensions: 10 20 30 40
```

## Sample Output

```text
Minimum number of multiplications: 18000
Time Complexity: O(n^3)
Execution Time: 0.000119 seconds

Because:
A1 = 10 × 20
A2 = 20 × 30
A3 = 30 × 40

Best order:
(A1 × A2) × A3

Cost:
(10 × 20 × 30) + (10 × 30 × 40)
= 6000 + 12000
= 18000
```

## Conclusion

The **Matrix Chain Multiplication Problem** is successfully implemented using Dynamic Programming. The algorithm efficiently finds the **minimum number of scalar multiplications** required to multiply a sequence of matrices.
